## Key Terms - Write Your Own Definition After Reading

| Term | Your Definition (In Your Own Words) |
|------|-------------------------------------|
| Chain-of-thought prompting | A method that can be used to improve LLMs' outputs. A coherent series of intermediate reasoning steps that lead to the final answer for a problem. |
| Zero-shot prompting | An LLM is given a command using natural language; no examples are provided (e.g., define standard deviation) |
| Few-shot prompting | An LLM is given a command using natural language and given multiple demonstrations of the task |
| Reasoning chain | This is part of the CoT process. Reasoning chains are included in the exemplars provided to the LLM to illustrate how to complete the task. |
| Emergent ability | Chain of Thought performance gains when used with models of ∼100B parameters |
| Hallucination | AI-generated content that sounds factual, but it is not |
| Intrinsic hallucinations | AI-generated content that contradicts source content |
| Extrinsic hallucinations | AI-generated content that cannot be verified using source content |

